WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.210
Isle de Jean Charles, in Louisiana,
once covered more than 8,900 hectares.

2
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:10.150
Today, only about 130 hectares remain.

3
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.510
Its people are moving to a new community,

4
00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:15.590
the New Isle, on higher ground inland.

5
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.750
Participation was voluntary.

6
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.690
So when is moving the best plan?

7
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:22.770
As soon as any flooding starts?

8
00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:27.010
In this mission, you'll compare the
ways people adapt to rising seas,

9
00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.490
from sea walls to raised
homes to moving away.

10
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.970
Then you'll see how the choice changes
between richer and poorer places,

11
00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:38.430
and when adaptation itself backfires.

12
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:43.470
Your mission: decide when moving away is
the best plan for a place facing rising

13
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:44.360
seas.
